hadiths[41]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24470","Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-Nahhas ibn Qahm Abu al-Khattab narrated to us, from Shaddad Abi Ammar al-Shami, he said: Awf ibn Malik said: O plague, take me to you. He said: They said: Have you not heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The longer the Muslim lives, the better it is for him? He said: Yes, but I fear six things: the rule of the foolish, the selling of judgment, the multitude of police, the severing of kinship, a generation that will emerge taking the Qur'an as flutes, and the shedding of blood."
"24471","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from Hisham ibn Yusuf, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: I sought permission from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Shall I enter, all of me or part of me? He said: Enter, all of you. I entered upon him while he was performing ablution, a lingering ablution. He said to me: O Awf ibn Malik, count six things before the Hour: the death of your prophet, take one. Then the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis. Then a death that will seize you, dying in it as sheep die. Then trials will appear, and wealth will increase until a single man is given one hundred dinars and is discontent with it. Then the Banu al-Asfar will come to you under eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand."
"24472","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, he said: Awf ibn Malik, he and Dhu al-Kala', entered the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis. Awf said to him: You have your cousin with you. Dhu al-Kala' said: Yet he is among the best, or among the most righteous of people. Awf said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: None narrates except a ruler, one commanded, or one who pretends."
"24473","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: al-Nahhas informed us, from Shaddad Abi Ammar, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, who said: O plague, take me to you. They said to him: Why do you say this? Have you not heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The believer's long life only increases him in good? He said: Yes, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Waki'."
"24474","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Azhar, meaning Ibn Sa'id, from Dhi al-Kala', from Awf ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: Storytellers are three: a ruler, one commanded, or one who is conceited."
"24475","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah, from Habib ibn Ubayd, he said: Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to me, from Awf, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray over a deceased person, and I understood from his prayer over him: O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, grant him health, pardon him, honor his abode, widen his entrance, wash him with water, snow, and hail, purify him of faults as You purified the white garment of filth, replace for him a home better than his home, a family better than his family, and a wife better than his wife, admit him into Paradise, save him from the Fire, and protect him from the punishment of the grave."
"24476","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us with a stick, and in the mosque there were hanging bunches, among them a bunch containing poor-quality dates. He prodded the bunch with the stick in his hand and said: If the owner of this charity wished, he could have given charity better than this. The owner of this charity will eat poor-quality dates on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Then he turned to us and said: By Allah, O people of Madinah, you shall leave it for forty years for the wild creatures. He said: I said: Allah knows best. He said, meaning: birds and beasts. He said: And we used to say: This is what the non-Arabs call al-karaki."
"24477","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Malih al-Hudhali narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abi al-Malih narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Burdah, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, that he was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey. He traveled with them the whole of their day without loosening a knot for them, and the whole of the night without loosening a knot except for prayer, until they stopped in the middle of the night. He said: A man watched the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he put down his saddle. He said: I came to him and looked, and I saw no one but asleep, and no camel but with its neck laid down, asleep. He said: I stretched and looked where the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had put his saddle, but I did not see him in his place. So I went out stepping over the saddles until I went out to the people, then I went on my way in the darkness of the night. I heard a bell, and I came to it, and there I was with Mu'adh ibn Jabal and al-Ash'ari. I came to them and said: Where is the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? And there was a humming like the humming of a millstone. I said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was at this sound. They said: Sit, be quiet. A little passed, then he came until he reached us. We stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we were frightened when we did not see you, so we followed your trail. He said: A comer from my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, came to me and gave me the choice between half of my ummah entering Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession. We said: We remind you of Allah and companionship, except that you make us among the people of your intercession. He said: You are among them. Then we went on, and a man and two men would come, and he would inform them of what he had informed us, and they would remind him of Allah and companionship, except that he make them among the people of his intercession, and he would say: You are among them. Until the people came to an end, and they crowded upon him and said: Make us among them. He said: I call you to witness that it is for whoever of my ummah dies not associating anything with Allah."
"24478","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq and Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Laqit, from Malik ibn Hidm, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, who said: We raided with Amr ibn al-As over us. We were afflicted with hunger, and we passed by people who had slaughtered a camel. I said: I will treat it for you on condition that you feed me some of it. And Ibrahim said: That you feed me from it. So I treated it, then I took what they gave me and brought it to Umar ibn al-Khattab, but he refused to eat it. Then I brought it to Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, and he said the like of what Umar ibn al-Khattab said, refusing to eat. Then I was sent to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, after that during the conquest of Makkah. He said: Are you the owner of the camel? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He did not add to that."
"24479","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi informed us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Tabuk at the end of the last part of the night, while he was in a tent, or he said: a dome of leather. He said: I asked, then I sought permission and said: Shall I enter? He said: Enter. I said: All of me? He said: All of you. He said: I entered, and there he was performing ablution, a lingering ablution."
"24480","Al-Hasan ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah, from Amr ibn Qays al-Kindi, that he heard Asim ibn Humayd say: I heard Awf ibn Malik say: I stood with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He began by using the tooth-stick, then performed ablution, then stood praying, and I stood with him. He began and opened with al-Baqarah, not passing by a verse of mercy but stopping and asking, nor passing by a verse of punishment but stopping and seeking refuge. Then he bowed and remained bowing as long as his standing, saying in his bowing: Glory be to the Owner of power, dominion, pride, and greatness. Then he recited Al Imran, then another surah, doing the like of that."
"24481","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir informed me, he said: Zurayq, the freedman of Banu Fazarah, narrated to me, from Muslim ibn Qarazah, and he was the cousin of Awf ibn Malik, he said: I heard Awf ibn Malik say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The best of your leaders are those whom you love and who love you, you supplicate for them and they supplicate for you. The worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and who hate you, you curse them and they curse you. We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not oppose them then? He said: No, as long as they establish prayer for you. And whoever has a ruler appointed over him and sees him committing something of disobedience to Allah, let him disapprove of what he commits of disobedience to Allah, and let him not withdraw a hand from obedience."
"24482","Haywah narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, he said: Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood among his companions and said: Do you fear poverty, need, or does this world concern you? For Allah will open for you the land of Persia and Rome, and this world will be poured upon you abundantly, so that nothing will turn you aside after me, if anything turns you aside, except it."
"24483","Haywah ibn Shurayh and Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, they said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Sayf, from Awf ibn Malik, that he narrated to them that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged between two men. The one judged against, when he turned away, said: Allah suffices me, and He is the best Disposer of affairs. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bring the man back to me. He said: What did you say? He said: I said: Allah suffices me, and He is the best Disposer of affairs. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah blames incapacity, but you must be shrewd. If a matter overcomes you, say: Allah suffices me, and He is the best Disposer of affairs."
"24484","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to us, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out one day, I being with him, until we entered the synagogue of the Jews in Madinah on a feast day of theirs. They disliked our entering upon them. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: O company of Jews, show me twelve men who will bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and Allah will remove from every Jew under the surface of the sky the anger that He is angry with him. He said: They fell silent; none of them answered him. Then he repeated to them, but none answered him. Then he said it a third time, but none answered him. He said: You have refused. By Allah, I am indeed the Gatherer, I am the Last, and I am the Chosen Prophet, whether you believe or disbelieve. Then he turned away, I being with him, until when we were about to go out, a man behind us called: Stay as you are, O Muhammad. He said: He turned, and that man said: What kind of man do you know me to be among you, O company of Jews? They said: By Allah, we do not know that there was among us a man more knowledgeable of the Book of Allah than you, nor more understanding than you, nor than your father before you, nor than your grandfather before your father. He said: I bear witness by Allah that he is the prophet of Allah whom you find in the Torah. They said: You have lied. Then they rejected his word and spoke evil of him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have lied; your word will not be accepted. Just now you praised him with the good you praised, and when he believed, you called him a liar and said of him what you said, so your word will not be accepted. He said: We went out, we being three: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I, and Abdullah ibn Salam. And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning him: Say: Have you considered, if it is from Allah and you disbelieve in it, while a witness from the Children of Israel has borne witness to the like of it and believed, while you were arrogant? Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people."
"24485","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to us, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, who said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and greeted him. He said: Awf? I said: Yes. He said: Enter. He said: I said: All of me or part of me? He said: Rather, all of you. He said: O Awf, count six things before the Hour, the first of them my death. He said: I wept until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began to quiet me. He said: I said: One. The second: the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis. I said: Two. The third: a pestilence that will be in my ummah, seizing them like the qu'as of sheep. He said: Three. The fourth: a trial that will be in my ummah, and he magnified it. Say: Four. The fifth: wealth will overflow among you until a man is given one hundred dinars and is discontent with it. Say: Five. The sixth: a truce that will be between you and the Banu al-Asfar, and they will march against you with eighty banners. I said: What is a banner? He said: A flag; under each flag twelve thousand. The camp of the Muslims that day will be in a land called al-Ghutah, in a city called Damascus."
"24486","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to us, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, who said: When spoils came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he would distribute them that same day. He gave the married one two shares and the unmarried one one share. We were called, and I was called before Ammar ibn Yasir. I was called and he gave me two shares, as I had a family. Then he called Ammar ibn Yasir, and he was given one share. A piece of a gold chain remained, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began lifting it with the tip of his stick, then raised it, saying: How will you be on the day much of this becomes abundant for you?"
"24487","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to me, from his father Jubayr, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, who said: We raided a raid toward the edge of Sham, with Khalid ibn al-Walid appointed over us. He said: A man from the reinforcements of Himyar joined us and lodged with us, having nothing with him but a sword, no weapon besides it. A man from the Muslims slaughtered a camel, and he kept scheming until he took from its hide something like a shield. He spread it on the ground, then kindled fire upon it until it dried, and made for it a holder like a buckler. It was decreed that we met our enemy, among them a mixture of Romans and Arabs from Quda'ah. They fought us fiercely, and among the people was a Roman man on a blond horse of his, with a gilded saddle, a belt stained with gold, and a sword like that. He kept charging at the people and inciting against them. That reinforcement man kept scheming for that Roman until he passed by him; he got behind him and struck the hock of his horse with the sword, so it fell. Then he followed it with strikes of the sword until he killed him. When Allah granted the victory, he came asking for the spoils, with people testifying for him that he was his killer. Khalid gave him some of his spoils and kept the rest. When he returned to the lodging of Awf, he mentioned it, and Awf said to him: Go back to him, and let him give you what remains. He went back to him, but he refused him. Awf walked until he came to Khalid and said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decreed the spoils for the killer? He said: Yes. He said: What prevents you from handing over to him the spoils of his slain man? Khalid said: I deemed it too much for him. Awf said: If I see the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I shall mention that to him. When he arrived in Madinah, Awf sent him to seek redress from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He called Khalid, with Awf sitting, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What prevents you, O Khalid, from handing over to this man the spoils of his slain man? He said: I deemed it too much for him, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Hand it over to him. He said: He passed by Awf, and Awf pulled his cloak and said: Let there be recompense for you for what I mentioned to you from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard him and became angry. He said: Do not give it to him, O Khalid. Will you not leave my commanders to me? The parable of you and them is like that of a man who was entrusted with camels or sheep: he pastured them, then chose their watering, brought them to a pond, and they waded into it, drank the clear water and left the turbid. Their clear is for you, and their turbid is upon them."
"24488","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to me, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i and Khalid ibn al-Walid, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not take a fifth from the spoils of the slain."
"24489","Al-Hasan ibn Sawwar Abu al-Ala' narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will never combine upon this ummah two swords: a sword from among themselves and a sword from their enemy."
"24490","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to me, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi, he said: Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to us, from Awf ibn Malik, that he said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day, he looked at the sky, then said: This is the time when knowledge is to be taken away. A man from the Ansar called Ziyad ibn Labid said to him: Will knowledge be taken away, O Messenger of Allah, while among us is the Book of Allah, and we have taught it to our children and our women? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I used to think you among the most understanding of the people of Madinah. Then he mentioned the straying of the people of the two Books, though they had with them what they had of the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Jubayr ibn Nufayr met Shaddad ibn Aws at the prayer place and narrated to him this hadith from Awf ibn Malik. He said: Awf spoke the truth. Then he said: Do you know what the removal of knowledge is? He said: I said: I do not know. He said: The departure of its vessels. He said: And do you know which knowledge is the first to be removed? He said: I said: I do not know. He said: Humility, until you can hardly see a humble person."
"24491","Ali ibn Abi Asim narrated to us, he said: al-Nahhas ibn Qahm informed me, from Abu Ammar Shaddad, from Awf ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has three daughters, three sisters, two daughters, or two sisters, fears Allah regarding them and treats them well until they separate or die, they will be a veil for him from the Fire."
"24492","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Abdullah, that Abdullah ibn Yazid, the storyteller of Maslamah, narrated to him that Awf ibn Malik narrated to him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: None narrates except a ruler, one commanded, or one who is conceited."
"24493","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Habib, from Rabi'ah ibn Laqit, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, who said: I entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among six, seven, or eight men. He said to us: Pledge allegiance to me. We said: O Prophet of Allah, we have already pledged allegiance to you. He said: Pledge allegiance to me. So we pledged allegiance to him, and he took upon us what he took upon the people. Then he followed that with a hidden word and said: Do not ask people for anything."
"24494","Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, that Ya'qub his brother and Ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Yazid, the storyteller of Maslamah at Constantinople, narrated to them from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: None narrates to people except a ruler, one commanded, or one who is conceited."
"24495","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Amr informed us, from Busr ibn Ubaydullah al-Hadrami, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded wiping over the khuffs in the raid of Tabuk: three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident."
"24496","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Ata' informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, who said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in a private chamber of his. I said: Shall I enter? He said: Enter. I said: All of me? He said: All of you. When I sat, he said: Withhold six things that will be before the Hour, the first of them the death of your prophet. He said: I wept. Hushaym said: I do not know with which of them he began. Then the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis, a trial entering the house of every hair and mud, wealth overflowing among you until a man is given one hundred dinars and is discontent with it, a pestilence among people like the qu'as of sheep. He said: And a truce between you and the Banu al-Asfar, and they will betray you, marching against you with eighty banners. Ya'la said: With sixty banners, under each banner twelve thousand."
"24497","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, who said: I went out with those who went out with Zayd ibn Harithah of the Muslims in the raid of Mu'tah, accompanied by a reinforcement man from Yemen with nothing but his sword. A man from the Muslims slaughtered a camel, and the reinforcement man asked him for a piece of its hide. He gave it to him, and he made it like a shield. We went on and met the hosts of Rome, among them a man on a blond horse of his, with a gilded saddle and gilded weapons. The Roman kept inciting against the Muslims, and the reinforcement man sat for him behind a rock. The Roman passed by him, so he hamstrung his horse, it fell, and he overcame him and killed him, taking his horse and weapons. When Allah granted victory to the Muslims, Khalid ibn al-Walid sent to him and took the spoils from him. Awf said: I came to him and said: O Khalid, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decreed the spoils for the killer? He said: Yes, but I deemed it too much. I said: You shall return it to him, or I shall inform of it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He refused to return it to him. Awf said: They gathered before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I related to him the story of the reinforcement man and what Khalid had done. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Khalid, what carried you to what you did? He said: O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I deemed it too much. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Khalid, return to him what you took from him. Awf said: He said: Take it, O Khalid, did I not fulfill for you? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is that? I informed him, and the Messenger of Allah became angry and said: O Khalid, do not return it to him. Will you leave my commanders to me? Yours is the clear part of their affair, and upon them is its turbid part."
"24498","Al-Walid said: I asked Thawr about this hadith, and he narrated to me from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, the like of it."
"24499","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid, meaning Abu Ja'far, he said: Salih ibn Abi Arib narrated to me, from Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us, or entered, while we were in the mosque, with a stick in his hand. A man had hung bunches of poor-quality dates, and he prodded with the stick into that bunch, then said: If the owner of this charity wished, he could have given charity better than this. The owner of this charity will eat poor-quality dates on the Day of Resurrection."
"24500","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Faraj ibn Fudalah informed us, from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid, from Muslim ibn Qarazah, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The best of you and the best of your leaders are those whom you love and who love you, you supplicate for them and they supplicate for you. The worst of you and the worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and who hate you, you curse them and they curse you. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not fight them? He said: No, as long as they pray the five for you. And whoever has a governor over him and sees him committing something of the disobediences of Allah, let him hate what he committed, and do not withdraw a hand from obeying him."
"24501","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Muawiyah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr from his father from Awf ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed over a dead person. He said: And I understood from his prayer over him: O Allah, forgive him and have mercy on him and wash him with water and ice, and cleanse him of sins as You cleansed the white garment of filth."
"24502","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Muawiyah ibn Salih from Azhar ibn Said from Dhu Kala from Awf ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The storytellers are three: a ruler, or one commanded, or a conceited one."
"24503","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us from Abu al-Malih from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, halted us for rest one night, and each man among us spread out the foreleg of his mount. He said: And I ended up at some of the camels, and behold the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with no one in front of it. He said: So I went out seeking the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and behold Muadh ibn Jabal and Abdullah ibn Qays standing. I said: Where is the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. They said: We do not know, except that we heard a sound at the top of the valley like the shaking of a saddle. He said: Stay a little. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us and said: A comer from my Lord came to me tonight and gave me choice between half of my ummah entering Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession. So we said: We adjure you by Allah and companionship that you make us among the people of your intercession. He said: Then you are among the people of my intercession. He said: So we turned to the people in crowds, and behold they had become frightened and had missed their Prophet. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A comer from my Lord came to me tonight and gave me choice between half of my ummah entering Paradise and intercession, and I chose intercession. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we adjure you by Allah and companionship that you make us among the people of your intercession. He said: So when they crowded upon him, he said: I make you witnesses that my intercession is for whoever of my ummah does not associate anything with Allah."
"24504","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on one of his journeys, and the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made his camel kneel, and we knelt with him, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: And between half of my ummah entering Paradise."
"24505","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Safwan ibn Amr from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr from his father from Awf ibn Malik who said: When fay came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he would divide it that same day, giving the married man two shares and giving the unmarried man one share."
"24506","Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid informed us, he said: Salih ibn Abi Arib narrated to us from Kathir ibn Murrah from Awf ibn Malik who said: Awf ibn Malik entered the mosque of Hims, and behold the people gathered around a man. He said: What is this gathering. They said: Kab is storytelling. He said: Woe to him, did he not hear the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: None tells stories except a ruler, or one commanded, or a conceited one."
"24507","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Al-Nahhas informed us from Shaddad Abu Ammar from Awf ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I and a woman with darkened cheeks will be like these two on the Day of Resurrection, and he joined his two fingers, the forefinger and the middle finger: A woman of rank and beauty widowed from her husband, who confined herself to her orphans until they separated or died."
"24508","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Al-Nahhas informed us from Shaddad Abu Ammar from Awf ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no Muslim servant who has three daughters and spends on them until they separate or die, except they will be for him a veil from the Fire. So a woman said: O Messenger of Allah, or two. He said: Or two."
"24509","Waki narrated to us from Al-Nahhas from Shaddad Abu Ammar from Awf ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I and a woman with darkened cheeks will be in Paradise like these two: A woman widowed from her husband who confined herself to her orphans until they separated or died."
"24510","Husayn narrated to us in the tafsir of Shayban from Qatadah, he said: A companion of ours narrated to us, I think him Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali, from Awf ibn Malik, and he mentioned it, and he said: Between half of my ummah entering Paradise. End of the Musnad of Awf ibn Malik al-Ansari, and it is the completion of the Musnad of the Ansar, may Allah be pleased with them."
